{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Leisure Time"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": " Go Fly a Kite"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 17}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe  routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le17ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Adverbs of Frequency"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Adverbs of frequency (always, usually, never, etc.) say how often something happens.<br />  Sometimes the adverb specifies the exact frequency of the action, like <span class=\"italic\">yearly</span> or <span class=\"italic\">daily</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": " They are usually placed before the verb. With verb tenses that have two parts, like the Present Continuous tense, they are placed between the auxiliary and the main verb."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Adverb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" How often?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" always\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 100%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"usually\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 60%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rarely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 10%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"never\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"0%\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "People often tend to visit some of the new kite stores that are regularly opening in big cities around the world.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Kite lovers always make a point of using kites for many reasons."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Adverbs of Manner"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use adverbs of manner to describe how something is done."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adverbs of manner should always come immediately after verbs which have no object (intransitive verbs)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <ul><li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">Kite lovers participate in lively...</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adverbs of manner can also be used after infinitives."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <ul><li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">It's important to drive carefully.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember that adverbs of manner are usually placed either after the main verb or after the object."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <ul><li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">People often tend to visit some of the new kite stores that are regularly opening in big cities around the world.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take into account that we can form adverbs from adjectives by adding <span class=\"italic\">-ly</span>, and when the adjective ends in <span class=\"strong\">y</span>, change it to <span class=\"italic\">\u2013ily</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "ready \u2013 readily"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<ul><li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">They can also subscribe to some of the many kite magazines that are readily available for kite lovers.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The adjectives <span class=\"italic\">fast</span>, <span class=\"italic\">hard</span>, <span class=\"italic\">well</span> and <span class=\"italic\">straight</span> do not change when they become adverbs."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "go fly a kite"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "go away; get out of here"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "exa